<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances rise in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances rose in the week that ended March 12, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Mar 12  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.61   -0.148    +0.780</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     8.85   +1.341    -1.349</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.66   +1.066    +5.731</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 129.00   +0.600   -30.800</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.97   -0.020    +2.109</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   Jan 97     Dec 96     Jan 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.63	69.74	59.28</p>
<p>M2					 394.80     398.32     388.67</p>
<p>M3					 497.80     500.53     472.55</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Jan	   Dec</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-16.27	-13.93</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     685.16	685.01</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.23	108.04</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
